        "original_id": "24ddfc8b-850a-5417-b921-ea1bf703029d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"Friends in Low Places\", \"No Fences\", \"The Thunder Rolls\", \"Mr. Blue\", \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home\"\n- People: Garth Brooks, Dewayne Blackwell, David Frizzell\n- Organizations: The Fleetwoods, Billboard\n- Topics: release dates, chart performance, songwriting credits\n\nFacts:\n- The Fleetwoods had a hit with \"Mr. Blue\" in 1959.\n- David Frizzell had a hit with \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home\" in 1982.\n- Garth Brooks performed \"Friends in Low Places,\" a song that became a hit in 1990.\n- \"Friends in Low Places\" was released on August 6, 1990 as the lead single from Garth Brooks's album \"No Fences.\"\n- \"No Fences\" was released on August 27, 1990.\n- Dewayne Blackwell wrote songs including \"Mr. Blue,\" \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home,\" and \"Friends in Low Places.\"\n- \"No Fences\" reached number 1 on Billboard's Top Country Albums chart.\n- \"The Thunder Rolls\" was released in April 1991 as the fourth and final single from Garth Brooks's album \"No Fences.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4141097c-c301-5dcd-803e-8a200da6b420",
        "text": "Page: Friends in Low Places. Sentence: \"Friends in Low Places\" is a song performed by American country pop artist Garth Brooks.\nPage: Friends in Low Places. Sentence: It was released on August 6, 1990 as the lead single from his album \"No Fences\".\nPage: No Fences. Sentence: It was released on August 27, 1990, and reached #1 on \"Billboard's\" Top Country Albums chart.\nPage: Dewayne Blackwell. Sentence: His songs include \"Mr. Blue\", a 1959 hit for the Fleetwoods; \"I'm Gonna Hire a Wino to Decorate Our Home\", a 1982 hit for David Frizzell; and \"Friends in Low Places\", a 1990 hit for Garth Brooks.\nPage: The Thunder Rolls. Sentence: It was released in April 1991 as the fourth and final single from his album \"No Fences\".",
